# XSH getc()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.getc.001
anchor     functions/getc.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/fgetc.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       On a stream reading the bytes 0x41, 0xff, 0x00, 0x42, successive
           getc() calls return 0x41, 0xff, 0 and 0x42, ftell() after each is
           1, 2, 3 and 4, and the next getc() returns EOF with feof() true.
test       t/001-bytes.c

assertion  XSH.getc.002
anchor     functions/getc.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/fgetc.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       On a stream reading "ab" whose end-of-file indicator is set,
           after "c" is appended through a separate open(), getc() returns
           EOF and feof() stays true; after clearerr() getc() returns 'c'.
test       t/002-eof-sticky.c

assertion  XSH.getc.003
anchor     functions/getc.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/fgetc.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
says       On a stream opened "r" whose descriptor was closed before the
           first read, getc() returns EOF, sets errno to EBADF and sets the
           stream's error indicator.
test       t/003-ebadf.c
